    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Tier 2 — Kabbalist</strong></p><p><strong>“You don’t hunt Sparks. You classify them — and classification is power.”</strong></p><p>At Tier 2, you stop mistaking mystery for depth. Most mysteries are just unlabeled containers. You bring labels.</p><p><strong>Strategic (Faction Scale)</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Identification Efficiency:</strong> once per scene of the Great Work's Identification phase, the marks cost or time to identify a required Spark drops by 25% (the card fires it).</li></ul><p><em>Mechanically, you waste fewer resources on the wrong answer. Narratively, the world stops wasting your time.</em></p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> every act of correct classification closes some other possibility. Expect rigidity, social friction, or backlash from people who preferred the ambiguity.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
